From: PowOS <mats@powback.com>
Subject: [PATCH] backends/anland: restore a minimized window when its task gains focus

Broforce's full-screen window can already be minimized when its Android
consumer connects. Raising and requesting focus leaves that window unmapped:
the Android task is foreground but black, while Steam retains keyboard focus.
Restore the window before raising it, just as activateWindow does, without
switching the desktop to the private task desktop.

--- a/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp
+++ b/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp
@@ -167,6 +167,7 @@
 void AnlandWindowTask::focus()
 {
     if (m_window && m_exported) {
+        m_window->setMinimized(false);
         // The window is shown (on the tasks desktop, which isn't current), so it can take the focus without a desktop
         // switch: requestFocus() neither raises nor switches (activateWindow() would switch to its desktop). Raised
         // too: every task's window lies at the same place on that desktop, and Xwayland gives a touch to the X window
